  <p class="eyebrow">The United Methodist Church</p>
  <h1>Regionalization</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">
    What the amendment says, paragraph by paragraph, with the text it replaces
    alongside it.
  </p>

  <p class="lede">
    In 2024 the General Conference adopted a constitutional amendment that puts
    every part of the church on the same footing. The annual conferences ratified
    it, and the Council of Bishops certified the result on 5 November 2025. It is
    now in force.
  </p>

  <p>
    Most published explanations describe the change without showing it. This site
    does the opposite. Every claim here is one click from the constitutional text
    that produces it, and where the text is ambiguous or the record incomplete,
    the page says so rather than smoothing it over.
  </p>

  <dl class="stat-row">
